Subject: [PATCH] fix: serve the site as HTML, not as a Markdown file
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GitHub Pages publishes this repository root, so README.md was the live website.
GitHub sanitises HTML in Markdown: every style attribute was stripped, the
YouTube iframe was escaped into visible source text, and the invented elements
(<p1>…<p9>, </hr>) were dropped — which is why the public page showed a literal
"<iframe width=..." block and a stray "p9 Copyright @2021" line under the footer.

- index.html now holds the site, where that markup is valid
- real elements and a <style> block replace <p1>…<p9> and </hr>
- the video is a click-to-load thumbnail: one image, no cookie until you choose to
  watch, and it still opens the video. An embed sets tracking cookies on load.
- adds lang, viewport (the page had none, so phones got a zoomed-out desktop
  layout), description and Open Graph tags
- fixes the dead instagtam.com link (now instagram.com/ssamahan_)
- fixes the 'mailto: link, which had a stray quote inside the href and so never
  opened a mail client
- moves the /c/ channel URL to the current /@handle form
- fixes 'Technogy' and 'iniated'
- README.md is now a real README explaining the site and how to edit it

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
